From dd64a5e16eed3c038302ba5c7cb2944f7073128b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 13:33:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Keep retrieved passages inside the context budget
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Asked "aké som mal operácie v minulosti", the assistant answered that the
system holds no record of any operation. It did: the card had just been
imported, retrieval ranked the right passage top with a score of 4.4 —
"Operácie a hospitalizácie: Operácia 27.1.93, Orchiopexia" — and the endpoint
that runs the same search returns it. The passage never reached the model.

The context is capped at a size, and the cap trims from the end. Importing a
99-page card multiplied the metric and trend sections; they now filled the
budget on their own, and the sections below them — the document list and the
passages retrieved for the question — were cut off. From the model's side the
profile looked like measurements and nothing else, which is exactly what it
said.

Ordering now reflects what is worth keeping: the passages and the document list
come before the per-metric sections, the trend list is capped, and the daily
aggregates stay last where the cap reaches them first. The budget goes to 20k.

The rendered size, the number of passages and the number of documents are now
logged. This failure is invisible from outside — the request succeeds, the
answer reads plausibly, and nothing says the context was cut short of the
evidence — so it needs a line in the log to be diagnosable at all.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SUjLLy2enx9LeWY7if66cK
